According to `GENERAL_AI_TRAINING_KNOWLEDGE.md` (CUDA OOM):

Potential causes:

- batch size;
- resolution;
- sequence length;
- model size;
- optimizer state;
- activations;
- fragmentation;
- worker duplication;
- validation memory;
- distributed replication.

Possible mitigations:

- smaller micro-batch;
- gradient accumulation;
- activation checkpointing;
- mixed precision;
- sharding;
- lower resolution;
- fewer workers;
- memory-aware validation.

